62) What is the difference between t-SNE and UMAP for dimensionality reduction?

They are both non-linear and iterative dimensionality reduction algorithms. t-SNE aims to minimize the KL-divergence when projecting the high-dimensional points to a lower dimension. Neighboring points in the high dimension should also neighbor in the low dimension space. t-SNE is known for not keeping a reliable global structure between clusters. UMAP creates a graph in the high dimension where strong links represent similar points in the high dimension space. During the optimization, nodes with weaker links can be moved further away and nodes with strong links tend to cluster. UMAP is known for keeping a more reliable global structure. 

63) How Random Number Generator Works, e.g. rand() function in python works?

Random number generators are in fact pseudo-random sequences that are calculated based on functions designed to approximate random. Given a seed, the random sequence is always the same (deterministic).

