66) What is the basic difference between LSTM and Transformers?

Those are fundamentally different architectures. LSTMs (Long short term memory) are recurrent nets with a very specific architecture that uses memories and gate mechanisms to incorporate past features into the folowing time step. Transformers are attention based architectures, they became popular for languaging modeling where the input in tokenized and inputed to blocks of attention layer followed by a feedforward layer. Transformers are often used to model sequences in a autoregressive manner. Given an input sequence, the next token is predicted, the prediction is appended to the input sequence for the prediction of the second token.

66) What are RCNNs?

Recurrent Convolutional NNs. They use convolution architectures for processing one time stamp (eg frame from a video) and the recurring architecture for processing the time dimension. 
